comments:
Until this is fixed and as a crude method to prevent the spikes on restarts.  I created two additional sensors for each ecobee sensor.  You can see the spikes when I was testing it earlier in the day.
```
- platform: statistics
  name: "ecobee Temperature statistics"
  entity_id: sensor.ecobee_temperature
  sampling_size: 40
  max_age: "00:05:00"
  precision: 1
  quantile_method: inclusive
- platform: template
  sensors:
    ecobee_temperature_calculated:
      friendly_name: "ecobee Temperature (calc)"
      device_class: temperature
      value_template: >
        {% if not is_state('sensor.ecobee_temperature_statistics', 'unknown') and states('sensor.ecobee_temperature_statistics') | float %}
          {% if ( (states.sensor.ecobee_temperature == states.sensor.ecobee_temperature_statistics) and (as_timestamp(now()) - as_timestamp(states.sensor.ecobee_temperature.last_changed | default(0))) | float < 300 ) %}
            {{ states.sensor.ecobee_temperature_statistics.state }}
          {% else %}
            {{ states.sensor.ecobee_temperature.state }}
          {% endif %}
        {% else %}
          {% if ( (as_timestamp(now()) - as_timestamp(states.sensor.ecobee_temperature.last_changed | default(0))) | float > 30 ) %}
            {{ states.sensor.ecobee_temperature.state }}
          {% else %}
            unknown
          {% endif %}
        {% endif %}
      icon_template: >
        {% if not is_state('sensor.ecobee_temperature_statistics', 'unknown') and states('sensor.ecobee_temperature_statistics') | float %}
          {% if ( (states.sensor.ecobee_temperature == states.sensor.ecobee_temperature_statistics) and (as_timestamp(now()) - as_timestamp(states.sensor.ecobee_temperature.last_changed | default(0))) | float < 300 ) %}
            mdi:thermometer-alert
          {% else %}
            mdi:thermometer
          {% endif %}
        {% else %}
          mdi:thermometer
        {% endif %}
      unit_of_measurement: "°F"
```
